$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=smshbad  LOC_AFTER=?

* Every bad prime p <_ X, one with a prime factor q of p - 1 above X ^c ( 1 - E ), is m q + 1 for a cofactor m <_ |_ X ^c E _| and a prime q <_ |_ X / m _| with m q + 1 prime: the bad primes lie in the range of the map ( m , q ) |-> m q + 1 on the tagged union of the twin sets (Lean: hbad_sub of smooth_shifted_weak).

